A containerized BIND instance is entirely reasonable. The important architectural requirement isn't "BIND" or "container"; it's:

> **A minimal authoritative DNS capability exists independently of VCF and enterprise AD/DNS and can resolve every name required to construct VCF.**

VCF is sensitive to DNS, and VCF Installer has explicit DNS-related configuration structures and validations. Broadcom also documents deployment failures when the Installer cannot obtain required DNS information. ([Broadcom Developer][2])

I'd have that container **start automatically when the recovery VM boots** and generate its zone data from our recovery configuration rather than maintaining a second hand-edited copy.

