Yes. I think you've just turned the **Recovery VM** into something more useful than a break-glass appliance: it becomes the **VCF bootstrap/recovery control point**.

Broadcom's model supports the core of this idea. VCF 9's Installer does not contain the product binaries and can consume them from a private offline depot; Broadcom describes that depot as a self-managed web server hosting the software repository. ([VMware Blogs][1]) So using Nginx on this VM to serve the VCF depot is architecturally reasonable.

The one thing I'd change in your wording is **"automatically download the latest binaries."** I would automate **discovery/download into staging**, but not automatically promote "latest" into the recovery baseline. Broadcom changed its download mechanism to authenticated/token-based downloads, so the pipeline will need to account for that, and a newly published bundle shouldn't become our disaster-recovery version until we've actually rebuilt the lab with it. ([VMware Blogs][2])

